-- Clean deep-well test deck for the adjoint well-objective gradient.
-- Three-phase (required by the adjoint TypeTag) but DEAD OIL + DRY GAS + WATER:
-- no DISGAS / no VAPOIL, so Rs = Rv = 0 always and there is NO reservoir-side
-- explicit cross-step quantity (no DRSDT/DRVDT/VAPPARS) and no hysteresis. The
-- gas-oil contact is above the reservoir, so there is no free gas. Single-well
-- control (no groups). Hence the ONLY explicitly-updated quantity in play is the
-- STANDARD-well frozen wellbore head (+ F0 + explicit B). A vertical producer
-- perforates a ~95 m column (large datum-to-perforation depth span), so the
-- frozen head is material: the StandardWell adjoint bhp gradient is biased,
-- while the multisegment one (--convert-to-multisegment-well) is exact.

RUNSPEC

TITLE
  DEEPWELL - clean deep multi-perforation well (dead oil / dry gas / water)

DIMENS
  3 3 20 /

OIL
WATER
GAS

METRIC

TABDIMS
  1 1 20 20 /

WELLDIMS
  2 20 1 2 /

WSEGDIMS
  2 25 20 /

START
  1 JAN 2020 /

EQLDIMS
  1 /

UNIFOUT

GRID

DX
  180*100 /
DY
  180*100 /
DZ
  180*5 /

TOPS
  9*2000 /

PORO
  180*0.2 /

PERMX
  180*100 /
PERMY
  180*100 /
PERMZ
  180*10 /

INIT

PROPS

-- dead oil (no dissolved gas)
PVDO
  150 1.05 1.1
  200 1.02 1.2
  300 1.00 1.4 /

-- dry gas (no vaporised oil)
PVDG
  150 0.0130 0.018
  200 0.0100 0.020
  300 0.0075 0.024 /

PVTW
  200 1.0 4.0E-5 0.5 0.0 /

DENSITY
  800 1000 1.0 /

ROCK
  200 4.0E-5 /

SWOF
  0.20 0.0   1.0  0.0
  0.40 0.05  0.5  0.0
  0.60 0.20  0.2  0.0
  0.80 0.50  0.05 0.0
  1.00 1.0   0.0  0.0 /

SGOF
  0.00 0.0   1.0  0.0
  0.20 0.05  0.5  0.0
  0.50 0.30  0.1  0.0
  0.80 0.70  0.0  0.0 /

SOLUTION

-- datum 2000, P=200 bar; OWC at 2110 (below reservoir base 2100 => no free
-- water); GOC at 2030 => a free-gas cap in the upper layers. The deep producer
-- then draws a mixture of free gas (low density) and oil (high density), so the
-- wellbore density is strongly state-dependent even though there is NO dissolved
-- gas (DISGAS off): a clean way to make the frozen StandardWell head biased.
EQUIL
  2000 200 2110 0 2030 0 1 0 0 /

SUMMARY

WBHP
/
WOPR
/
WWPR
/
FPR

SCHEDULE

WELSPECS
  'PROD' 'G1' 2 2 2000 'OIL' /
  'INJ'  'G1' 1 1 2000 'WATER' /
/

COMPDAT
  'PROD' 2 2 1 20 'OPEN' 1* 1* 0.15 /
  'INJ'  1 1 1 20 'OPEN' 1* 1* 0.15 /
/

WCONPROD
  'PROD' 'OPEN' 'ORAT' 80 4* 50 /
/

WCONINJE
  'INJ' 'WATER' 'OPEN' 'RATE' 100 1* 400 /
/

TSTEP
  10 10 10 10 10 10 10 10 10 10 /
